    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0220" n="1288" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg1288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Conference files, lot 60 D 627, CF 370</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the United States Acting
                        Permanent Representative on the North Atlantic Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Martin</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d99-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1954-09-27">September 27,
                            1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>Participants:</label>
                    <item>The Secretary</item>
                    <item>General Gruenther
                    </item>
                    <item>Ambassador Aldrich
                    </item>
                    <item>Mr. Merchant
                    </item>
                    <item>Mr. McCardle
                    </item>
                    <item>Mr. Bowie
                    </item>
                    <item>Mr. Martin
                    </item>
                    <item>Colonel Silver
                    </item>
                    <item>Colonel Richardson
                    </item>
                    <item>Mr. O’Connor
                    </item>
                </list>
                <list rendition="#flush" subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>
                        SACEUR Assistance in Alternative
                        Arrangements to EDC
                    </item>
                </list>
                <p>General Gruenther called attention
                    to the fact that during the morning meeting<anchor n="2" xml:id="d99-f2"/> he
                    had not had an opportunity to answer the question asked by the Secretary about
                    the feasibility of establishing a strategic <pb facs="0221" n="1289"
                        xml:id="pg1289"/> zone in which it would be militarily unwise to produce
                    certain types of munitions.</p>
                <p>General Gruenther stated that
                    establishment of such a zone was feasible, and his Headquarters would be willing
                    to assist in it. However, they would prefer not to get involved, and he
                    suggested that it might be possible to utilize, at least as a solution for the
                    present, the arrangements in this regard agreed to in connection with the EDC negotiations.</p>
                <p>General Gruenther expressed the
                    opinion that the Germans were apparently willing to accept the EDC solution although he doubted the prohibition of
                    the production in Germany of military aircraft could be maintained for long.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d99-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d99-f1-content">
                <p>The source text was circulated to members of the U.S. Delegation to the
                    Nine-Power Conference as document NPT Memo
                    30.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d99-f2" n="2" xml:id="d99-f2-content">
                <p>For a record of this morning meeting, see the memorandum of conversation by
                        Moore, Sept. 27, <ref
                        target="#pg1281">p. 1281</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
